{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01JO", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$g : Y \\to S$", "MATH_0003": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0004": "$X \\times_S Y \\to Y$", "MATH_0005": "$X \\to S$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{I} \\subset \\mathcal{O}_S$", "MATH_0007": "$X \\times_S Y \\to Y$", "MATH_0008": "$\\Im(g^*\\mathcal{I} \\to \\mathcal{O}_Y)$", "MATH_0009": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0010": "$X \\times_S Y \\to Y$", "MATH_0011": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0012": "$X \\times_S Y \\to Y$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-fibre-product-immersion}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:69e1a6ad127cf7b97907c20fcbe47888f5c64980e8fe6a4ec788927441c37a50", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d5e1f8b68f3426bd0e2c7f1d293ed6f03a212b35ecb21e85ea8c11127005950d", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> and <MATH_0002> be morphisms of schemes\nwith the same target.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> If <MATH_0003> is a closed immersion,\nthen <MATH_0004> is a closed immersion.\nMoreover, if <MATH_0005> corresponds to the quasi-coherent\nsheaf of ideals <MATH_0006>, then\n<MATH_0007> corresponds to the sheaf of ideals\n<MATH_0008>.\n<STRUCT_0003> If <MATH_0009> is an open immersion,\nthen <MATH_0010> is an open immersion.\n<STRUCT_0004> If <MATH_0011> is an immersion,\nthen <MATH_0012> is an immersion.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0b5c2c6dc1aad9b29d828c7cad674f788320906fed9b969523091601695ad30c", "unit_id": "tag:01JU:statement"}
{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01JO", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{I} \\subset \\mathcal{O}_S$", "MATH_0003": "$Z \\subset Y$", "MATH_0004": "$\\Im(g^*\\mathcal{I} \\to \\mathcal{O}_Y)$", "MATH_0005": "$Z$", "MATH_0006": "$Z = X \\times_S Y$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-restrict-map-to-closed}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-closed-subspace-scheme}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-open-fibre-product}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c8c07382854b88b3f9748bc184aeda7b62011a536e182a1e31515ca29b0ded8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5043ca9a5138fadb998d1ac6090e16b9d10cd32e2630f2ff8828e6b798f92e73", "source_text": "Assume that <MATH_0001> is a closed immersion corresponding\nto the quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals <MATH_0002>.\nBy Lemma <REF_0001> the closed subspace\n<MATH_0003> defined by the sheaf of ideals\n<MATH_0004> is the fibre product\nin the category of locally ringed spaces.\nBy Lemma <REF_0002> <MATH_0005> is a scheme.\nHence <MATH_0006> and the first statement follows.\nThe second follows from Lemma <REF_0003>\nfor example. The third is a combination of\nthe first two.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7eb1afb0cc2e9e8e72eb2aa75bdbd7aa3d3c8dd28ffc9866e351684936d05c24", "unit_id": "tag:01JU:proof"}
{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "01JO", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$Z \\subset Y$", "MATH_0003": "$Y$", "MATH_0004": "$f^{-1}(Z)$", "MATH_0005": "$Z$", "MATH_0006": "$Z \\times_Y X$", "MATH_0007": "$X$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-fibre-product-immersion}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-inverse-image-closed-subscheme}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:0443c99c3fa8e534f4ffa2b71f012822b30657e5281bbadc52da1dd75e477404", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:cff979ea3342f48d9cf2f3ddbf2525474c4c256a8bf9e085defa82083d0ec27f", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes. Let <MATH_0002> be a\nclosed subscheme of <MATH_0003>. The <TEXTITOPEN_0001>inverse image <MATH_0004> of the\nclosed subscheme <MATH_0005><TEXTITCLOSE_0001> is the closed subscheme <MATH_0006> of\n<MATH_0007>. See Lemma <REF_0001> above.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6bdd2260e949e7792987c6186f212dc3def431291d856d6e46665c244447193a", "unit_id": "tag:01JV:statement"}
{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01JO", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:39a8300456f97d8c2ba04e0e7a4b06d0f7f95242ac8580d29d8729bcf816d802", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe may occasionally also use this terminology with locally closed and\nopen subschemes.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:52422eb4c6ad3291ee91d3eec9e28e12690361f02b835058bb1ba5b040bd3c81", "unit_id": "tag:01JO:prose-0005"}
